<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cvetković–Maček Agreement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1939">1939</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cvetković–Maček Agreement was a political settlement reached on 26 August 1939 between the Yugoslav prime minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dragisa-cvetkovic">Dragiša Cvetković</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladko-macek">Vladko Maček</a>, leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatian-peasant-party">Croatian Peasant Party</a>, with the backing of the regent Prince Paul. It created the autonomous Banovina of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, with its own ban and a planned assembly, and brought Maček into the government as deputy prime minister. It was opposed by Serbian nationalists and by the separatist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ustase">Ustaše</a>.</p></div>
